invariant: INV-48
file: mldsa_sign_steps.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mldsa-vector
reason: the signer's and key generation's rows of A run on sha3.c under
  every value, so a session with CH_CPU_AVX2 signs at the speed of the
  loops. The keys and signatures stay the same, so bin/mldsa_runtime_test
  counts the calls into the four-way sampler under every value. Only an
  x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds the binary for
  x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and
  this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    if (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX2) {
        return mlds_matrix_row_avx2(cpu, row, rho, i, v_hat);
--- new
    if (cpu & 0U) {
        return mlds_matrix_row_avx2(cpu, row, rho, i, v_hat);
